      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        164,
        1666,
        1977,
        1840
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "The City's health insurance program has been expanded over the past several months so that it provides a choice of plans for large segments of City employees with whom collective bargaining negotiations were recently completed. Other groups of employees may be granted this choice as negotiations are completed with their representatives.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2237,
          "min": -1.337
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 54,
          "mean": -0.0001,
          "min": -0.0046
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 4161,
        "area_px": 297968,
        "density": 0.01396,
        "chars": 338,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 81.23
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        164,
        1874,
        2000,
        2220
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "As a further extension of my program for fostering health insurance coverage for City employees, arrangements have been made with the various health insurance carriers to continue such coverage on the retirement of employees enrolled in a City sponsored plan. While the retiree will bear the full cost of the premium payments, through deductions from his pension allowance, there will be substantial benefits for him since he would be entitled to the lower group rate, and he will be able to obtain coverage not available to direct payment subscribers. Two groups of retirees are to be covered under this program:",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2018,
          "min": -1.5333
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 108,
          "mean": -0.0002,
          "min": -0.01
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 7229,
        "area_px": 595452,
        "density": 0.01214,
        "chars": 613,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 84.8
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        270,
        2247,
        1815,
        2465
      ],
      "category": "List-item",
      "text": "**Group I** - Employees enrolled under the choice of health plans at the time of retirement who retire after January 1, 1965, and those enrolled under the regular (HIP-Blue Cross) plan at the time of retirement who retire after July 1, 1965. These retirees will retain their membership in the group of active City employees.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.25,
          "min": -1.388
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 2,
          "mean": -0.0016,
          "min": -0.0032
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 76,
          "mean": -0.0082,
          "min": -0.5754
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 3615,
        "area_px": 337040,
        "density": 0.01073,
        "chars": 324,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 89.63
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        270,
        2492,
        1840,
        2721
      ],
      "category": "List-item",
      "text": "**Group II** - Employees who retired prior to January 1, 1965 or July 1, 1965, depending on whether they were under the choice of health plans, and who continued their coverage by direct payments to the insurance carrier. These retirees will be formed into a group separate from active City employees.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.1992,
          "min": -1.3041
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 2,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 69,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0008
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 1210,
        "area_px": 358110,
        "density": 0.00338,
        "chars": 301,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 248.76
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        164,
        2745,
        2015,
        2981
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "The Personnel Director, as administrator for the City's health insurance program, is hereby authorized and directed to establish regulations and procedures for implementing this policy on continuing health insurance coverage for eligible retirees. All department and agency heads are requested to cooperate with the Personnel Director in carrying out this program.",
